  ('ev_wiki_chief-joseph_1855_6', 'ent_chief-joseph', NULL, 1855, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'The 1855 reservation maintained much of the traditional Nez Perce lands, including Joseph''s Wallowa Valley.[5] It is recorded that the elder Joseph requested that Young Joseph protect their 7.7-millio', 'The 1855 reservation maintained much of the traditional Nez Perce lands, including Joseph''s Wallowa Valley.[5] It is recorded that the elder Joseph requested that Young Joseph protect their 7.7-million-acre homeland, and guard his father''s burial place.[6]  In 1863, however, an influx of new settlers, attracted by a gold rush, led the government to call a second council.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
