  ('ev_wiki_chris-cornell_1988_8', 'ent_chris-cornell', NULL, 1988, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'Though the band was being courted by major labels, they signed to independent label SST Records in 1988 to release their debut album, Ultramega OK, for which they earned a Grammy Award nomination for ', 'Though the band was being courted by major labels, they signed to independent label SST Records in 1988 to release their debut album, Ultramega OK, for which they earned a Grammy Award nomination for Best Metal Performance in 1990.[27] The band subsequently signed with A&M Records, becoming the first grunge band to sign to a major label.[20]  In 1989, Soundgarden released their second effort and their first album for a major label, Louder Than Love.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
