   'Bush to his Council on Service and Civic Participation.[6]  Early life and education  Roberts was born in New Orleans.[7] She received the nickname Cokie from her brother, Tommy, who as a child could ', 'Bush to his Council on Service and Civic Participation.[6]  Early life and education  Roberts was born in New Orleans.[7] She received the nickname Cokie from her brother, Tommy, who as a child could not pronounce her given name, Corinne.[8]  Her parents were Lindy Boggs and Hale Boggs, each of whom served for decades as Democratic members of the House of Representatives from Louisiana; Lindy succeeded Hale after his plane disappeared over Alaska in 1972.[9] Cokie was their t', 'src_en_wikipedia',
