  ('ev_wiki_cole-porter_1937_22', 'ent_cole-porter', '1937-10-24', 1937, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'After a walking tour of Europe with his friends, Porter returned to New York in October 1937 without her.[76] They were soon reunited by an accident Porter suffered.[77]  On October 24, 1937, Porter w', 'After a walking tour of Europe with his friends, Porter returned to New York in October 1937 without her.[76] They were soon reunited by an accident Porter suffered.[77]  On October 24, 1937, Porter was riding with Countess Edith di Zoppola and Duke Fulco di Verdura at Piping Rock Club in Locust Valley, New York, when his horse rolled on him and crushed his legs, leaving him substantially crippled and in constant pain for the rest of his life.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
