  ('ev_wiki_cole-porter_1940_24', 'ent_cole-porter', NULL, 1940, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'Porter spent time in Hollywood, New York and Williamstown.[90]  1940s and postwar  Fred Astaire in You''ll Never Get Rich Panama Hattie (1940) was Porter''s longest-running hit so far, running in New Yo', 'Porter spent time in Hollywood, New York and Williamstown.[90]  1940s and postwar  Fred Astaire in You''ll Never Get Rich Panama Hattie (1940) was Porter''s longest-running hit so far, running in New York for 501 performances despite the absence of any enduring Porter songs.[91] It starred Merman, Arthur Treacher and Betty Hutton.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
