   'The critics scoffed, but the film was a huge success, chiefly because of the wealth of vintage Porter numbers in it.[98] The biopic''s success contrasted starkly with the failure of Vincente Minnelli''s', 'The critics scoffed, but the film was a huge success, chiefly because of the wealth of vintage Porter numbers in it.[98] The biopic''s success contrasted starkly with the failure of Vincente Minnelli''s film The Pirate (1948), with Judy Garland and Gene Kelly,[99] in which five new Porter songs received little attention.[100]  Porter and Jean Howard in early 1954 From this low spot, Porter made a conspicuous comeback in 1948 with Kiss Me, Kate.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
