   'The five warrior cousins were three brothers, Flying Hawk, Kicking Bear, and Black Fox II, all sons of Chief Black Fox, also known as Great Kicking Bear, and two other cousins, Eagle Thunder and Walki', 'The five warrior cousins were three brothers, Flying Hawk, Kicking Bear, and Black Fox II, all sons of Chief Black Fox, also known as Great Kicking Bear, and two other cousins, Eagle Thunder and Walking Eagle.[80][d] On September 4, 1877, Young Black Fox commanded Crazy Horse''s warriors in the latter''s absence—a display of courage that earned him the regard of both Lakota and white observers alike.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
