  ('ev_wiki_edward-hopper_1939_30', 'ent_edward-hopper', NULL, 1939, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'He and his wife kept a detailed ledger of their works noting such items as "sad face of woman unlit", "electric light from ceiling", and "thighs cooler".[75]  For New York Movie (1939), Hopper demonst', 'He and his wife kept a detailed ledger of their works noting such items as "sad face of woman unlit", "electric light from ceiling", and "thighs cooler".[75]  For New York Movie (1939), Hopper demonstrated his thorough preparation with more than 53 sketches of the theater interior and the figure of the pensive usherette.[76]  The effective use of light and shadow to create mood is also central to Hopper''s methods.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
