  ('ev_wiki_edward-hopper_1916_32', 'ent_edward-hopper', NULL, 1916, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'He painted the majority of the pure seascapes between 1916 and 1919 on Monhegan Island.[79] Hopper''s The Long Leg (1935) is a nearly all-blue sailing picture with the simplest of elements, while his G', 'He painted the majority of the pure seascapes between 1916 and 1919 on Monhegan Island.[79] Hopper''s The Long Leg (1935) is a nearly all-blue sailing picture with the simplest of elements, while his Ground Swell (1939) is more complex and depicts a group of youngsters out for a sail, a theme reminiscent of Winslow Homer''s iconic Breezing Up (A Fair Wind) (1876).[80]  Urban architecture and cityscapes were also major subjects for Hopper.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
