  ('ev_wiki_edward-hopper_1925_33', 'ent_edward-hopper', NULL, 1925, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'He was fascinated with the American urban scene, "our native architecture with its hideous beauty, its fantastic roofs, pseudo-gothic, French Mansard, Colonial, mongrel or what not, with eye-searing c', 'He was fascinated with the American urban scene, "our native architecture with its hideous beauty, its fantastic roofs, pseudo-gothic, French Mansard, Colonial, mongrel or what not, with eye-searing color or delicate harmonies of faded paint, shouldering one another along interminable streets that taper off into swamps or dump heaps."[81]  In 1925, he produced House by the Railroad.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
