   'Forty years later, Lavinia said that because their mother was chronically ill, one of the daughters had to remain always with her.[76] Dickinson took this role as her own, and "finding the life with h', 'Forty years later, Lavinia said that because their mother was chronically ill, one of the daughters had to remain always with her.[76] Dickinson took this role as her own, and "finding the life with her books and nature so congenial, continued to live it".[76]  Withdrawing more and more from the outside world, Dickinson began in the summer of 1858 what would be her lasting legacy.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
