   'He expanded and reworked the material, and eventually published it as Reason: the Only Oracle of Man.[20]  Heman remained in Salisbury where he ran a general store until his death in 1778, but Allen''s', 'He expanded and reworked the material, and eventually published it as Reason: the Only Oracle of Man.[20]  Heman remained in Salisbury where he ran a general store until his death in 1778, but Allen''s movements are poorly documented over the next few years.[21] He lived in Northampton, Massachusetts, in the spring of 1766, where his son Joseph was born and where he invested in a lead mine.[22] The authorities asked him to leave Northampton in July 1767, though no official rea', 'src_en_wikipedia',
