   'On September 10, 1962, while staying with friend Mary Tucker, Hamer was shot at 15 times in a drive-by shooting by racists.[14][27][28] No one was injured in the event.[11] The next day, Hamer and her', 'On September 10, 1962, while staying with friend Mary Tucker, Hamer was shot at 15 times in a drive-by shooting by racists.[14][27][28] No one was injured in the event.[11] The next day, Hamer and her family evacuated to nearby Tallahatchie County[9] for three months, fearing retaliation by the Ku Klux Klan because she had attempted to vote.[29][17][30]  I guess if I''d had any sense, I''d have been a little scared—but what was the point of being scared?', 'src_en_wikipedia',
