   'After 1/4 of the population died of tuberculosis,[57] the Chiricahuas, including Geronimo, were relocated to Fort Sill, Oklahoma, in 1894; they built villages scattered around the post based on kindre', 'After 1/4 of the population died of tuberculosis,[57] the Chiricahuas, including Geronimo, were relocated to Fort Sill, Oklahoma, in 1894; they built villages scattered around the post based on kindred groups.[59] Geronimo, like other Apaches, was given a plot of land on which he took up farming activities.[60] On the train ride to Fort Sill, many tourists wanted a memento of Geronimo, so they paid 25 cents for a button that he cut off his shirt or a hat he took off his head.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
