  ('ev_wiki_grant-wood_1910_3', 'ent_grant-wood', NULL, 1910, 'narrative_death', 'narrative',
   'After graduating from Washington High School, he enrolled in The Handicraft Guild, an art school run entirely by women in Minneapolis in 1910.[citation needed]  In 1913, Wood enrolled at the School of', 'After graduating from Washington High School, he enrolled in The Handicraft Guild, an art school run entirely by women in Minneapolis in 1910.[citation needed]  In 1913, Wood enrolled at the School of the Art Institute of Chicago, where he studied from 1913 to 1916.[6] Wood also performed some work as a silversmith.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
