  ('ev_wiki_grant-wood_1934_7', 'ent_grant-wood', NULL, 1934, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'He became a great proponent of regionalism in the arts,[11] lecturing throughout the country on the topic.[12] As Wood''s classically American image was solidified, his bohemian days in Paris were expu', 'He became a great proponent of regionalism in the arts,[11] lecturing throughout the country on the topic.[12] As Wood''s classically American image was solidified, his bohemian days in Paris were expunged from his public persona.[13]  In 1934, Wood was offered a position working and teaching in Iowa City as Director of a New Deal Public Works of Art Project (PWAP).', 'src_en_wikipedia',
