   'William Rose Benét wrote that, with The Bridge, Crane "failed in creating what might have been a truly great poem" but that it "reveals potencies in the author that may make his next work even more re', 'William Rose Benét wrote that, with The Bridge, Crane "failed in creating what might have been a truly great poem" but that it "reveals potencies in the author that may make his next work even more remarkable".[1] His last work, "The Broken Tower" (1932), was unfinished and published posthumously.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
