   'Crane has been praised by several playwrights, poets, and literary critics, including Robert Lowell, Derek Walcott, Tennessee Williams, and Harold Bloom; Bloom called him "a High Romantic in the era o', 'Crane has been praised by several playwrights, poets, and literary critics, including Robert Lowell, Derek Walcott, Tennessee Williams, and Harold Bloom; Bloom called him "a High Romantic in the era of High Modernism".[2][3][4] Allen Tate called Crane "one of those men whom every age seems to select as the spokesman of its spiritual life; they give the age away."[1]  Life  Early life  Crane was born in Garrettsville, Ohio, on July 21, 1899 to Clarence A.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
