  ('ev_wiki_hart-crane_1930_13', 'ent_hart-crane', NULL, 1930, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'The Bridge (1930)  Main article: The Bridge  The first known mention of The Bridge was in a 1923 letter to Gorham Munson in which he wrote:   I am ruminating on a new longish poem under the title of T', 'The Bridge (1930)  Main article: The Bridge  The first known mention of The Bridge was in a 1923 letter to Gorham Munson in which he wrote:   I am ruminating on a new longish poem under the title of The Bridge which carries on further the tendencies manifest in ''F and H.'' It will be exceedingly difficult to accomplish it as I see it now, so much time will be wasted in thinking about it.[5]  Crane moved to Paterson, New Jersey, in 1927.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
