  ('ev_wiki_hart-crane_1929_16', 'ent_hart-crane', '1929-02', 1929, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'He managed to convince her to send him the money and left for Europe towards late November[5] intending to live in Mallorca, but instead went first to London then to Paris.[5] In Paris in February 192', 'He managed to convince her to send him the money and left for Europe towards late November[5] intending to live in Mallorca, but instead went first to London then to Paris.[5] In Paris in February 1929, Harry Crosby, who with his wife Caresse Crosby owned the fine arts press Black Sun Press, offered Crane the use of their country retreat, Le Moulin du Soleil in Ermenonville.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
