   'When Peggy Cowley, wife of his friend Malcolm Cowley, agreed to a divorce, she joined Crane.[16] The two began a romantic relationship on December 25, 1931.[5] As far as is known, she was his only het', 'When Peggy Cowley, wife of his friend Malcolm Cowley, agreed to a divorce, she joined Crane.[16] The two began a romantic relationship on December 25, 1931.[5] As far as is known, she was his only heterosexual partner.[16] "The Broken Tower", one of his last published poems, emerged from that affair.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
