   'Return to Concord, 1837–1844  The traditional professions open to college graduates—law, the church, business, medicine—did not interest Thoreau,[35]: 25  so in 1835 he took a leave of absence from Ha', 'Return to Concord, 1837–1844  The traditional professions open to college graduates—law, the church, business, medicine—did not interest Thoreau,[35]: 25  so in 1835 he took a leave of absence from Harvard, during which he taught at a school in Canton, Massachusetts, living for two years at an earlier version of today''s Colonial Inn in Concord.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
