   'Gansevoort''s entries include books Melville used for Moby-Dick and Clarel, including "Parsees—of India—an excellent description of their character, and religion and an account of their descent—East In', 'Gansevoort''s entries include books Melville used for Moby-Dick and Clarel, including "Parsees—of India—an excellent description of their character, and religion and an account of their descent—East India Sketch Book p. 21".[44] Other entries are on Panther, the pirate''s cabin, and storm at sea from James Fenimore Cooper''s The Red Rover.[45]  Work as a school teacher  The Panic of 1837 forced Gansevoort to file for bankruptcy in April.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
