  ('ev_wiki_jack-kerouac_1943_5', 'ent_jack-kerouac', NULL, 1943, 'narrative_death', 'narrative',
   'While at Columbia, Kerouac wrote several sports articles for the student newspaper, the Columbia Daily Spectator, and joined the Phi Gamma Delta fraternity.[28][29] He was a resident of Livingston Hal', 'While at Columbia, Kerouac wrote several sports articles for the student newspaper, the Columbia Daily Spectator, and joined the Phi Gamma Delta fraternity.[28][29] He was a resident of Livingston Hall and Hartley Hall, where other Beat Generation figures lived.[30][31] He also studied at The New School.[32]  Early adulthood  Kerouac''s Naval Reserve Enlistment photograph, 1943 When his football career at Columbia ended, Kerouac dropped out of the university.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
