  ('ev_wiki_jack-kerouac_1942_6', 'ent_jack-kerouac', '1942-10', 1942, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'Burroughs.[33][34][35]  During World War II, Kerouac was a United States Merchant Mariner from July to October 1942 and served on the SS Dorchester before its maiden voyage.[36] A few months later, th', 'Burroughs.[33][34][35]  During World War II, Kerouac was a United States Merchant Mariner from July to October 1942 and served on the SS Dorchester before its maiden voyage.[36] A few months later, the SS Dorchester was sunk during a submarine attack while crossing the Atlantic, and several of his former shipmates were lost.[36] In 1943 he joined the United States Navy Reserves.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
