   'Owens traveled the world and spoke to companies such as the Ford Motor Company and stakeholders such as the United States Olympic Committee.[95] In 1972, he and his wife retired to Arizona.[96]  Owens', 'Owens traveled the world and spoke to companies such as the Ford Motor Company and stakeholders such as the United States Olympic Committee.[95] In 1972, he and his wife retired to Arizona.[96]  Owens initially refused to support the black power salute by African-American sprinters Tommie Smith and John Carlos at the 1968 Summer Olympics.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
