   'In London, Astor at once made a contract with the North West Company, which from Montreal rivaled the trade interests of the Hudson''s Bay Company, then based in London.[15]  Astor imported furs from M', 'In London, Astor at once made a contract with the North West Company, which from Montreal rivaled the trade interests of the Hudson''s Bay Company, then based in London.[15]  Astor imported furs from Montreal to New York and shipped them to Europe.[16] By 1800, he had amassed over a quarter of a million dollars[17] (equivalent to about $470 million in 2025)[4] and had become one of the leading figures in the fur trade.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
   'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Jacob_Astor', 0.7, 10, 'en', 'YEAR', unixepoch(), unixepoch());
