   'After John''s older sister died at the age of two, his mother, Mary Newbold Sargent (née Singer, 1826–1906), suffered a breakdown, and the couple decided to go abroad to recover.[2] They remained nomad', 'After John''s older sister died at the age of two, his mother, Mary Newbold Sargent (née Singer, 1826–1906), suffered a breakdown, and the couple decided to go abroad to recover.[2] They remained nomadic expatriates for the rest of their lives.[7][8] Although based in Paris, Sargent''s parents moved regularly, spending seasons at the sea and at mountain resorts in France, Germany, Italy, and Switzerland.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
