   'Weir met Sargent in 1874 and noted that Sargent was "one of the most talented fellows I have ever come across; his drawings are like the old masters, and his color is equally fine".[22] Sargent''s exce', 'Weir met Sargent in 1874 and noted that Sargent was "one of the most talented fellows I have ever come across; his drawings are like the old masters, and his color is equally fine".[22] Sargent''s excellent command of French and his superior talent made him both popular and admired.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
