  ('ev_wiki_john-singer-sargent_1882_13', 'ent_john-singer-sargent', NULL, 1882, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'The Spanish master''s spell is apparent in Sargent''s The Daughters of Edward Darley Boit, 1882, a haunting interior that echoes Velázquez''s Las Meninas.[34] As in many of his early portraits, Sargent c', 'The Spanish master''s spell is apparent in Sargent''s The Daughters of Edward Darley Boit, 1882, a haunting interior that echoes Velázquez''s Las Meninas.[34] As in many of his early portraits, Sargent confidently tries different approaches with each new challenge, here employing both unusual composition and lighting to striking effect.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
