   'During his playing career, he wrote From Behind the Plate, published in 1972,[92] the instructional book Catching and Power Hitting in 1975,[93] and Catch You Later, an autobiography published in 1979', 'During his playing career, he wrote From Behind the Plate, published in 1972,[92] the instructional book Catching and Power Hitting in 1975,[93] and Catch You Later, an autobiography published in 1979 co-authored with William Brashler.[94] In 1999, he wrote The Complete Idiot''s Guide to Baseball.[95] In 2008, he co-wrote Catch Every Ball: How to Handle Life''s Pitches with Paul Daugherty.[96]  Bench has acted several times, usually related to his baseball career.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
