  ('ev_wiki_joni-mitchell_2002_1', 'ent_joni-mitchell', NULL, 2002, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'Rolling Stone, in 2002, named her "one of the greatest songwriters ever",[2] and AllMusic, in a 2011 biography, stated "Joni Mitchell may stand as the most important and influential female recording a', 'Rolling Stone, in 2002, named her "one of the greatest songwriters ever",[2] and AllMusic, in a 2011 biography, stated "Joni Mitchell may stand as the most important and influential female recording artist of the late 20th century."[1]  Mitchell began singing in small nightclubs in Saskatoon and throughout western Canada, before moving on to the nightclubs of Toronto.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
