   'His album The Köln Concert, released in 1975, is the best-selling piano recording in history.[2][3] In 2008, he was inducted into the DownBeat Jazz Hall of Fame in the magazine''s 73rd Annual Readers'' ', 'His album The Köln Concert, released in 1975, is the best-selling piano recording in history.[2][3] In 2008, he was inducted into the DownBeat Jazz Hall of Fame in the magazine''s 73rd Annual Readers'' Poll.[4]  In 2003, Jarrett received the Polar Music Prize and was the first recipient to be recognized with the prizes for both contemporary and classical music.[5] In 2004, he received the Léonie Sonning Music Prize.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
