   'Linux   Main article: History of Linux  The first Linux prototypes were publicly released on the Internet in late 1991 from an FTP server at his university.[8][21] Version 1.0 was released on 14 March', 'Linux   Main article: History of Linux  The first Linux prototypes were publicly released on the Internet in late 1991 from an FTP server at his university.[8][21] Version 1.0 was released on 14 March 1994.[22]  Torvalds first encountered the GNU Project in the autumn of 1991 when another Swedish-speaking computer science student, Lars Wirzenius, took him to the Helsinki University of Technology to listen to free-software guru Richard Stallman''s speech.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
