   'She is also the host of the Amazon Prime Video reality television series Lizzo''s Watch Out for the Big Grrrls, for which she won the Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Competition Program.[2] In 201', 'She is also the host of the Amazon Prime Video reality television series Lizzo''s Watch Out for the Big Grrrls, for which she won the Primetime Emmy Award for Outstanding Competition Program.[2] In 2019, Time named Lizzo "Entertainer of the Year" for her meteoric rise and contributions to music.[3] In addition to four Grammy Awards, she has also won a Billboard Music Award, a BET Award, and two Soul Train Music Awards.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
