   'She rejected the high school nearest her home, complaining that the chemistry lab was "just like a kitchen sink".[24] She eventually enrolled in Hyde Park High School but spent a miserable semester, f', 'She rejected the high school nearest her home, complaining that the chemistry lab was "just like a kitchen sink".[24] She eventually enrolled in Hyde Park High School but spent a miserable semester, for which a yearbook caption noted: "A.E.—the girl in brown who walks alone".[25]  Amelia Earhart graduated from Hyde Park High School in 1916.[26] Throughout her childhood, she had continued to aspire to a future career.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
