   'In the final game of the CBA series, Johnson had 30 points, 17 rebounds, and 13 assists, leading the All-Stars to a 126–121 victory over the Oklahoma City Cavalry.[148] By the time he returned to the ', 'In the final game of the CBA series, Johnson had 30 points, 17 rebounds, and 13 assists, leading the All-Stars to a 126–121 victory over the Oklahoma City Cavalry.[148] By the time he returned to the Lakers in 1996, the Magic Johnson All-Stars had amassed a record of 55–0, and Johnson was earning as much as $365,000 per game.[41] Johnson played with the team frequently over the next several years, with possibly the most memorable game occurring in November 2001.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
   'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Magic_Johnson', 0.7, 14, 'en', 'MONTH', unixepoch(), unixepoch());
