   'Although Twain initially spoke out in favor of American interests in the Hawaiian Islands, he later reversed his position,[6] going on to become vice president of the American Anti-Imperialist League ', 'Although Twain initially spoke out in favor of American interests in the Hawaiian Islands, he later reversed his position,[6] going on to become vice president of the American Anti-Imperialist League from 1901 until his death in 1910, coming out strongly against the Philippine–American War and American colonialism.[7][8][9] Twain published a satirical pamphlet, "King Leopold''s Soliloquy", in 1905 about Belgian atrocities in the Congo Free State.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
