   'Rogers also managed Twain''s money until all his creditors were paid.[75]: 188 [76]  Twain accepted an offer from Robert Sparrow Smythe[77] and embarked on a year-long around-the-world lecture tour in ', 'Rogers also managed Twain''s money until all his creditors were paid.[75]: 188 [76]  Twain accepted an offer from Robert Sparrow Smythe[77] and embarked on a year-long around-the-world lecture tour in July 1895[78] to pay off his creditors in full, although Twain was no longer under any legal obligation to do so.[79] It was a long, arduous journey, and he was sick much of the time, mostly from a cold and a carbuncle.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
