  ('ev_wiki_sylvia-plath_1956_13', 'ent_sylvia-plath', '1956-06-16', 1956, 'narrative_birth', 'narrative',
   'Then it just grew out of that, I guess, a feeling that we both were writing so much and having such a fine time doing it, we decided that this should keep on.[28]   Plath described Hughes as "a singer', 'Then it just grew out of that, I guess, a feeling that we both were writing so much and having such a fine time doing it, we decided that this should keep on.[28]   Plath described Hughes as "a singer, story-teller, lion and world-wanderer" with "a voice like the thunder of God".[4]  The couple were married only four months after they met, on June 16, 1956, at St George the Martyr in Holborn, London, and in honor of Bloomsday, with Plath''s mother as the sole witness.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
