  ('ev_wiki_sylvia-plath_1953_20', 'ent_sylvia-plath', '1953-08-24', 1953, 'narrative_death', 'narrative',
   'They found Plath dead with her head on the oven door, having sealed the kitchen door and the room upstairs with her sleeping children inside with tape, towels, and cloths.[42] She was 30 years old.[43', 'They found Plath dead with her head on the oven door, having sealed the kitchen door and the room upstairs with her sleeping children inside with tape, towels, and cloths.[42] She was 30 years old.[43]  Before her death, Plath had tried at least once to take her own life.[44] On August 24, 1953, she overdosed on sleeping pills.[45] In June 1962, she drove her car off the side of the road into a nearby clearing after learning about Hughes'' and Wevill''s affair.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
