   'Early years  Wilton Norman Chamberlain was born on August 21, 1936, in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, the sixth of nine children to southerners Olivia Ruth (née Johnson), a domestic worker, and William C', 'Early years  Wilton Norman Chamberlain was born on August 21, 1936, in Philadelphia, Pennsylvania, the sixth of nine children to southerners Olivia Ruth (née Johnson), a domestic worker, and William Chamberlain, a welder and handyman.[1][2] The family lived in a middle-class neighborhood in the Haddington section of West Philadelphia.[3] Chamberlain was raised as a Baptist.[4]  Chamberlain''s first competitive sport was track.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
