  ('ev_wiki_alice-paul_1916_16', 'ent_alice-paul', NULL, 1916, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'Paul formed the Congressional Union for Woman Suffrage and, later the National Woman''s Party (NWP) in 1916.[19]  The NWP began introducing some of the methods used by the suffrage movement in Britain ', 'Paul formed the Congressional Union for Woman Suffrage and, later the National Woman''s Party (NWP) in 1916.[19]  The NWP began introducing some of the methods used by the suffrage movement in Britain such as silent sentinels and focused entirely on achieving a constitutional amendment for woman suffrage.[16] Alva Belmont, a multi-millionaire socialite at the time, was the largest donor to Paul''s efforts.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
