   'News of her penniless state reached friends, and a fund for indigent Quakers quickly aided Paul.[10] Paul died at the age of 92 on July 9, 1977, at the Greenleaf Extension Home[59] a Quaker facility i', 'News of her penniless state reached friends, and a fund for indigent Quakers quickly aided Paul.[10] Paul died at the age of 92 on July 9, 1977, at the Greenleaf Extension Home[59] a Quaker facility in Moorestown, New Jersey, less than a mile from her birthplace and childhood home.[5] She is buried at Westfield Friends Burial Ground in Cinnaminson, New Jersey.[60] Visitors frequently leave notes at her tombstone to thank her for her lifelong work on behalf of women''s rights.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
