   'The Golden Gate Bridge is described in Frommer''s travel guide as "possibly the most beautiful, certainly the most photographed, bridge in the world".[9][10] At the time of its opening in 1937, it was ', 'The Golden Gate Bridge is described in Frommer''s travel guide as "possibly the most beautiful, certainly the most photographed, bridge in the world".[9][10] At the time of its opening in 1937, it was both the longest and the tallest suspension bridge in the world, titles it held until it was overtaken by the 1964 Verrazzano–Narrows Bridge and the 1998 Akashi Kaikyo Bridge, respectively.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
