  ('ev_wiki_central-park_1811_12', 'plc_central-park', NULL, 1811, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'These were seen as escapes from the noise and chaotic life in the city, which at the time was almost entirely centered on Lower Manhattan.[36] The Commissioners'' Plan of 1811, the outline for Manhatta', 'These were seen as escapes from the noise and chaotic life in the city, which at the time was almost entirely centered on Lower Manhattan.[36] The Commissioners'' Plan of 1811, the outline for Manhattan''s modern street grid, included several smaller open spaces but not Central Park.[37] As such, John Randel Jr. had surveyed the grounds for the construction of intersections within the modern-day park site.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
