   'Construction commenced on Belvedere Castle, Harlem Meer, and structures on Conservatory Water and the Lake.[138][146]  1870–1876: completion  Gentry in the new park, c. 1870 The Tammany Hall political', 'Construction commenced on Belvedere Castle, Harlem Meer, and structures on Conservatory Water and the Lake.[138][146]  1870–1876: completion  Gentry in the new park, c. 1870 The Tammany Hall political machine, which was the largest political force in New York at the time, was in control of Central Park for a brief period beginning in April 1870.[147] A new charter created by Tammany boss William M.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
