  ('ev_wiki_central-park_1880_18', 'plc_central-park', NULL, 1880, 'narrative_death', 'narrative',
   'The needles are so named because they were later moved to in front of the Caesarium in Alexandria, a temple originally built by Cleopatra VII of Egypt in honor of Mark Antony.[450] The needle in Centr', 'The needles are so named because they were later moved to in front of the Caesarium in Alexandria, a temple originally built by Cleopatra VII of Egypt in honor of Mark Antony.[450] The needle in Central Park arrived in late 1880 and was dedicated early the following year.[447][449]  The Strawberry Fields memorial, near Central Park West and 72nd Street,[5] is a memorial commemorating John Lennon, who was murdered outside the nearby Dakota apartment building.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
