  ('ev_wiki_central-park_1967_22', 'plc_central-park', NULL, 1967, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'The signals were coordinated so that drivers could go through all of the green lights if they maintained a steady speed of 25 miles per hour (40 km/h).[460][508] The drives were experimentally closed ', 'The signals were coordinated so that drivers could go through all of the green lights if they maintained a steady speed of 25 miles per hour (40 km/h).[460][508] The drives were experimentally closed to automotive traffic on weekends beginning in 1967, for exclusive use by pedestrians and bicyclists.[509] In subsequent years, the scenic drives were closed to automotive traffic for most of the day during the summer.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
