  ('ev_wiki_hollywood-sign_1923_1', 'plc_hollywood-sign', NULL, 1923, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'It was originally erected in 1923 as a temporary advertisement for a local real estate development, and spelled out "HOLLYWOODLAND" in 50-foot-tall (15.2 m) white uppercase letters in a word 450 feet ', 'It was originally erected in 1923 as a temporary advertisement for a local real estate development, and spelled out "HOLLYWOODLAND" in 50-foot-tall (15.2 m) white uppercase letters in a word 450 feet (137.2 m) long.[1] Due to increasing recognition, the sign was left up; the last four letters "LAND" were removed in 1949.[2] The sign was entirely replaced in 1978, using 45-foot-tall (13.7 m) letters in a more durable all-steel structure with concrete footings.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
