  ('ev_wiki_hollywood-sign_1923_4', 'plc_hollywood-sign', '1923-07-13', 1923, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'Since the last section, about 70 meters long, was very steep, the transport had to be done with pack animals.[12]  The sign was officially dedicated on 13 July 1923,[13] intended to last only a year a', 'Since the last section, about 70 meters long, was very steep, the transport had to be done with pack animals.[12]  The sign was officially dedicated on 13 July 1923,[13] intended to last only a year and a half.[14] The rise of American cinema in Los Angeles during the Golden Age of Hollywood gave it widespread visibility, causing it to be left beyond that,[15] for over a quarter of a century still spelling "Hollywoodland".', 'src_en_wikipedia',
