   'In September 1932, 24-year-old actress Peg Entwistle died by suicide by climbing a workman''s ladder up to the top of the ''H'' and jumping to her death.[16][17]  The sign’s illumination was switched off', 'In September 1932, 24-year-old actress Peg Entwistle died by suicide by climbing a workman''s ladder up to the top of the ''H'' and jumping to her death.[16][17]  The sign’s illumination was switched off in about 1933, as the new owners decided it was too expensive.[18]  Deterioration and restoration  In the 1970s, the sign reached its most dilapidated state.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
