  ('ev_wiki_independence-hall_1824_7', 'plc_independence-hall', NULL, 1824, 'narrative', 'narrative',
   'Constitution was debated, drafted, and ratified.[4]  In 1824, the building was renamed the Hall of Independence when it hosted the Marquis de Lafayette .[5]  In 1915, former U.S. president William How', 'Constitution was debated, drafted, and ratified.[4]  In 1824, the building was renamed the Hall of Independence when it hosted the Marquis de Lafayette .[5]  In 1915, former U.S. president William Howard Taft presided over a convention at Independence Hall, where the League to Enforce Peace was formed.[6]  The National Park, of which Independence Hall is a part, surrounds it and acts as a buffer zone between the building and the modern urban fabric.', 'src_en_wikipedia',
